    "html_url": "https://github.com/romaine-life/kill-me/commit/32d5d81ac902c623112aa187b3a7fe563a6c5ee1",
    "message": "fix: scope current-day settings reads/writes to the authenticated user\n\nThe `settings` document read in `GET /api/current-day` and the log-workout\nauto-advance queried `SELECT * FROM c WHERE c.type='settings'` with no userId\nfilter and used an arbitrary cross-partition `settings[0]`. After the\nMSAL -\u003e auth.romaine.life migration left workout data (and a stale settings\ndoc) under a legacy `microsoft|...` userId, that stale doc (currentDay=1)\nkept winning, so the app perpetually suggested Day 1 (Legs) even after Day 1\nwas logged.\n\n- GET /api/current-day: dedupe by most-recent `updatedAt` and coerce to Number\n- log-workout auto-advance: scope the settings lookup to `c.userId = req.user.sub`\n  (partition-keyed), always upsert with `id = settings_\u003cuserId\u003e` so a stray/legacy\n  doc id can't spawn a duplicate, and coerce day comparison/increment to Number\n- PUT /api/current-day: coerce incoming currentDay to Number so a string can\n  never be persisted\n\nProduction data was separately consolidated onto the current auth.romaine.life\nuserId (duplicate settings docs collapsed to one, currentDay=2).",
